      "id": "alg1",
      "text": "1: Input video V V , model encoder ℰ \\mathcal{E} and decoder 𝒟 \\mathcal{D} . 2: F ← ℰ ⁡ ( V ) F\\leftarrow\\mathcal{E}(V) ⊳ \\triangleright Compute Global Scene Representation 3: G ← { false } T × H × W G\\leftarrow\\{\\textbf{false}\\}^{T\\times H\\times W} ⊳ \\triangleright Initialize Occupancy Grid 4: 𝒯 ← ∅ \\mathcal{T}\\leftarrow\\emptyset ⊳ \\triangleright Initialize Set of Dense Tracks 5: while any ( G = false G=\\textbf{false} ) do 6: Sample a batch B B of unvisited source points from G G 7: for each ( u , v , t src ) ∈ B (u,v,t_{\\text{src}})\\in B do ⊳ \\triangleright Process batch in parallel 8: Q ← { u , v , t src , t tgt = t cam = k } k = 1 T Q\\leftarrow\\{u,v,t_{\\text{src}},{t_{\\text{tgt}}{=}t_{\\text{cam}}}{=}k\\}_{k=1}^{T} ⊳ \\triangleright Get Track Queries 9: P ← { 𝒟 ⁡ ( 𝐪 k , F ) } k = 1 T P\\leftarrow\\{\\mathcal{D}(\\mathbf{q}_{k},F)\\}_{k=1}^{T} ⊳ \\triangleright Run the decoder 10: G ← Visible ​ ( P ) G\\leftarrow\\text{Visible}(P) ⊳ \\triangleright Set visible track pixels as visited 11: 𝒯 ← 𝒯 ∪ P \\mathcal{T}\\leftarrow\\mathcal{T}\\cup P ⊳ \\triangleright Add new track to the output 12: end for 13: end while 14: return 𝒯 \\mathcal{T} Algorithm 1 Efficient Dense Tracking of All Pixels.",
