      "id": "S2.F3",
      "text": "Figure 3 : Pose accuracy vs . speed – We compare pose accuracy vs . throughput against recent state-of-the-art methods. Pose accuracy is 1 – error , averaged over ATE/RTE/RPE on Sintel and ScanNet. Throughput is measured in FPS on an A100 GPU. D4RT achieves 200+ FPS pose estimation, 9 × \\times faster than VGGT, and 100 × \\times faster than MegaSaM, while delivering superior accuracy.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "id": "S3.F4",
      "text": "Input video MegaSaM [ 29 ] π 3 \\pi^{3} [ 54 ] SpatialTrackerV2 [ 56 ] D4RT (Ours) Figure 4: Reconstruction results across methods – Pure reconstruction methods (MegaSaM and π 3 \\pi^{3} ) are only able to accumulate point clouds of all pixels; exhibiting clear failure cases in dynamic scenes. For example, the swan is repeated in MegaSaM’s reconstruction, and π 3 \\pi^{3} is failing entirely to reconstruct the flower. SpatialTrackerV2, a state-of-the-art tracking method, successfully captures dynamics, however its design only allows tracking points from one frame, leaving gaps in the reconstruction (behind the swan and train). D4RT is the only method that successfully reconstructs a full 4D representation of the scene including all pixels of the video.",
